hadiths[235]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1890","This tradition is also narrated along with another document."
"1891","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not required on wealth until one year has passed."
"1892","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on wealth until one year has passed on it."
"1893","This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) along with another chain of transmission."
"1894","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on property until it remains with its owner for one year."
"1895","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Radiyallahu Anhu says that when a person acquires wealth, Zakat on it is not halal (i.e. not obligatory) until one year has passed."
"1896","Abdullah bin Waqid narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to receive half a dinar out of every twenty dinars and one dinar out of every forty dinars (i.e. two and a half percent of zakat)."
"1897","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that no payment is required for 190 dirhams."
"1898","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take a quarter of a tenth of every forty dirhams (i.e. two and a half percent)."
"1899","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, that zakat is not required on wheat and dates until they reach the amount of five wasqs, and on silver, zakat is not required until it reaches five ounces, and on camels, zakat is not required until they reach five camels."
"1900","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that zakat is not required on silver less than five ounces, zakat is not required on less than five camels, and zakat is not required on dates less than five wasq."
"1901","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on less than five ounces of silver, Zakat is not required on less than five camels, and Zakat is not required on dates that are less than five vasaqs."
"1902","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: Zakat is not required for less than five camels, no payment is required for less than forty goats, no payment is required for less than thirty cows, no payment is required for less than twenty shekels of gold, no payment is required for less than two dirhams (of silver), no payment is required for less than five Wasq (of grain), while usher dates are not required. ``Grapes'' ``Wheat'' which will be collected from that which is irrigated naturally will require payment of usher and that which is irrigated (artificially) by means of dol will require payment of half of usher."
"1903","Sayyiduna Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he instructed him not to accept anything from a piece (of gold or silver) 'When the silver reaches two dirhams, to accept five dirhams from it,' not to accept anything more than that until it reaches forty dirhams,' when it reaches forty dirhams, then to accept one dirham from it (i.e. for every forty dirhams). receiving one). One of the narrators of this hadith is Humanhal bin Jarrah, whose surname is Abu Atuf, while his name is Jarrah bin Minhal. A narrator named Ibn Ishaq has copied his name in reverse."
"1904","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) to Yemen and asked him: What have you been ordered to do? He said, ""I have been ordered to receive one Tabi Tabi'a from every thirty cows and one Masna from every forty cows."" He was asked: ""Have you been given any orders about opportunities?"" He replied, ""No!"" I will ask the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this. (ie no payment will be required). The narrator describes; It means an animal that is between two years old and the words mean that nothing will be taken from it."
"1905","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his father. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro was asked about gems, pearls, precious stones, small pearls (or Abyssinian pearls) and plants that grow in the ground such as pearls, jewels, silk, vegetables that grow from the ground, pickled cucumbers, etc. He said that Zakat is not required on any stone and no Zakat is required on vegetables either. Wasallam only prescribed the payment (of Ushar) in wheat, barley, dates and grapes."
"1906","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) both state that the payment of zakat on dates and date-palm trees is not required until they reach five Wasaqs."
"1907","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this with reference to Sayyidna Ali Bin Abu Talib (RA) The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables, Zakat will not be required on “Araya” (Zakat will not be required on grains less than five wasaqs), Zakat will not be required on factors, and Zakat will not be required on the forehead. A narrator named Saqr bin Habib narrates that Pashani means horse, mule and slave."
"1908","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that vegetables that grow from the ground do not require Zakat."
"1909","Sayyidna Muhammad bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When he sent Sayyidna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) to Yemen, he instructed him to collect one dinar out of every forty dinars, collect five dirhams out of every two dirhams, and zakat is not required on less than five wasaqs, zakat is not required on less than five camels, and zakat is not required on vegetables."
"1910","Musa bin Talha narrates this statement of his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables."
"1911","Musa bin Talha narrates this on the authority of his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables."
"1912","Musa bin Talha narrates this from Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables. The narrator of this tradition, Marwan Sanjari, is weak."
"1913","Musa bin Talhah narrates this about Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1914","Musa bin Talha narrates that we have a letter of Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (Radi Allahu Anhu) in which it is written that the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) received zakat from wheat, raisins and dates."
"1915","Musa bin Talha narrated this in reference to the martyrs of Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him: the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that the land on which the sky is Baal (a palm tree planted near water so that the tree itself gets watered by underground water) and watered by flowing water (i.e. canal, etc.) will be required to pay usher, and the land that is watered by sprinkling (i.e. artificially) I will have to pay half-usher. Payment of Zakat will be required on dates, wheat, grains, but it is waived on cucumbers, watermelons, apples, kasab and other vegetables."
"1916","Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on vegetables."
"1917","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with regard to the martyrs of Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1918","This same tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to Sayyidna Mu'adhbin Jabal (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
"1919","Musa bin Talha narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade collecting zakat from vegetables."
"1920","The same hadith has been narrated by Sayyiduna Mu'adhbin Jabal (RA) on the authority of Musa bin Talha along with another chain of transmission."
"1921","Abu Burda' narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Musa Ash'ari (RA) and Sayyidna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) when the Prophet (PBUH) sent these two men to Yemen, and they both taught the people about the religious rules, (and he said) You people should only receive Zakat from these four things which are 'wheat', raisins and dates."
"1922","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this: Zakat is not required on any field (agricultural produce) until it reaches five wasqs. When it reaches five wasqs, then payment of zakat will be required on it, and one wasq is sixty sa’s. It is equal to a dirham."
"1923","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that Zakat should not be collected from a field (i.e. agricultural produce) until its yield is five Wasaq."
"1924","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: I have forgiven you the zakat of your slaves and horses, but you should bring your silver, agricultural produce and animal zakat."
"1925","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this as a hadith transmitted to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that zakat will not be required for less than five wasaqs, and one wasaq is equal to sixty Makhtums."
"1926","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on less than five Wasaqs and one Wasaq is sixty Sa'ahs."
"1927","Taus narrates that a calf was brought to the service of Sayyidna Mu'adh Radiyallahu Anhu, and he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) did not give me any order about it. The narrator narrates that their number was less than 30."
"1928","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu’adh (RA) to Yemen, he ordered him to receive one tabi’ or one tabiyyah from every thirty cows and receive one masna from every forty cows. So he said, ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give me any order about this. When I go to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I will inquire from him."" Then when Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him about the calf, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said that no payment will be required for it. A narrator named Mas'udi narrates that when their number is less than thirty, when the number of cows is from forty to sixty, two tabi'ahs will be required, when they reach seventy, one masna will be paid, and when they reach eighty, then two masna will be required, and when they reach ninety, three tabi's will be required. Masoudi says that the word ""Awq"" is written with ""s""."
"1929","Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent him to Yemen, he said, ""You receive grain (in zakat) from grain, from goats you receive goats from camels zakat, from camels zakat you receive camels, and from cows you receive zakat from cows."""
"1930","Sayyiduna Mu'adhbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the people of Yemen: ""You bring to me on Thursdays and twenty-one, and I will collect Zakat from you."" Amrunami narrator has quoted these words, you bring me wide clothes. This hadith is transmitted because the narrator named Taus has not found the time of Sayyidna Mu'adh."
"1931","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Muqathis were not among the things that Sayyiduna Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) brought."
"1932","Malik bin Aws narrates that once we were sitting near Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him. Meanwhile, Sayyidna Abu Zar Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, came to him and greeted him. He replied, ""I am fine."" Then he went to a pillar and stood. People also got up and went towards him and surrounded him. ""I was also among those who surrounded him."" People said: O Abu Dharr! If you tell us a hadith about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Zakat is required on camels, Zakat is required on goats, Zakat is required on cows, and Zakat is required on linen (silk). The narrator says he mentioned this word with ""z""."
"1933","Malik bin Awf narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Dharghafari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Zakat is required on camels, Zakat is required on goats, Zakat is required on cows, and on silk, Zakat is obligatory. If kept, it will be counted as a treasure through which it will be tarnished on the Day of Resurrection."
"1934","Malik bin Aws narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Zakat is given on camels, Zakat is given on goats, Zakat is given on cows, and Zakat is given on sheep.”"
"1935","Sayyiduna Mu'adbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to Yemen and instructed them to collect one tabi' or one tabi'ah from every thirty camels, and one masna from every forty cows, and from every adult person to collect a dinar equal to it."
"1936","This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the narrators have disagreed about one of its words."
"1937","Sayyiduna Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to Yemen and instructed them to collect one tabi or one tabiyya from every thirty cows and one masna from every forty cows and to collect one dinar from every adult person for it."
"1938","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Zakat is not required on domestic camels."
"1939","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on cows for domestic use, but one Tabi' is required for every thirty cows and one Masna for every forty cows."
"1940","Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that nothing is necessary in a cow for domestic use. In another tradition, the words are slightly different."
"1941","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on cows for domestic use."
"1942","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a cow used for farming does not require zakat."
"1943","Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates, ""I was staying with Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him."" After that, he mentioned a word. Then he also said that one day he heard Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said that (in order to avoid the collection of zakat, one should not separate the collected property and not collect the separate property). It will go and there will be two groups of people who will share about the tank, the shepherd and the animal to be given for marriage."
"1944","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required in Mushirah (that is, it is used for driving cows)."
"1945","Ibn Juraj narrates, I asked Ata about such people who have shares with each other, if they have 40 goats, then one goat will be required to be paid for all of them. So he said that one goat will be required to be paid for both of them."
"1946","Hameed bin Hilal narrates that a person brought a scripture to Hasan Basri in which various problems were written. He asked him about this scripture. He did not find any mistakes in these problems."
"1947","Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghaflah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person who received zakat from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. I sat by his side. A man brought a camel with a high hump and said: You accept it. He refused to accept it."
"1948","Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghaflah (RA) narrates that a person who received Zakat from the Prophet (PBUH) came to us. I sat next to him. I asked him what is written in your handwriting. He told him not to separate the wealth and not to collect the separate wealth (says the narrator) Then a man came to him with a camel with a high hump and he refused to accept it."
"1949","Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghafla (RA) narrates that a person came to us to receive Zakat from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The narrator narrates that I read in his writings that separate wealth should not be collected and that separate wealth should not be separated to avoid zakat (payment or collection). Refused to accept the camel. He said: If I received it from the wealth of a Muslim, then what would I do in the presence of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but there is some difference in it."
"1950","Ata narrates that Sayyidah Umm Salamah (RA) was wearing a gold necklace. She asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""When you pay his Zakat, it will not be counted; its meaning is the same."""
"1951","Abdullah bin Shaddad narrates: We came to the service of Sayyida Ayesha, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me, and he saw silver bracelets in my hand. Where did they come from? I said, I have made them so that I can wear them and come in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired whether you have paid his zakat. I did not submit! (or whatever Allah willed) then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""These are enough for you in Hell."" A narrator named Muhammad bin Ata is unknown."
"1952","Imam Shaabi narrates: I heard Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (RA) narrating that I brought a chain in the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that contained seventy pounds of gold. I said, O Messenger of Allah! You collect zakat from it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) collected one mithaqal and three-fourths of a mithqal from it."
"1953","This hadith has been narrated along with another document, however, these words are extra in it. I said, O Messenger of Allah! Is there any right in wealth apart from zakat? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! Then he recited the verse ""And he gives of his wealth of his own choice."""
"1954","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays Radiyallahu Anha narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam)."
"1955","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) says that there is no Zakat on jewelry, the narrator of this tradition, Abu Hamza, his name is Maymun, and this is a weak hadeeth."
"1956","Sayyid Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that there is no harm in wearing ornaments when their Zakat is paid."
"1957","Amro bin Shoaib cites this statement of his grandfather regarding his father, he wrote this letter to his secretary Salim asking him to pay zakat every year on the ornaments of his daughters."
"1958","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Masood) narrates that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “I have some jewels and my husband is a poor man. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! This tradition is an illusion. It is correct. This tradition is related to Ibrahim."
"1959","Alqamah narrates that the wife of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) asked her about her jewels, and he said, ""If they are worth two hundred dirhams, zakat must be paid on them."" She said, ""My nephews are under my care. Shall I spend it on them?"" So Syedna Abdullah replied yes! This tradition is ""suspended""."
"1960","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not obligatory on the property of a slave until he is freed."
"1961","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, ""Two women from Yemen came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."" They were wearing gold bracelets. He answered no! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then both of you should fulfill his right. There are these words in a hadith, they were both wearing gold bracelets. It also has these words (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then both of you pay the right for it. It is obligatory on you (the narrator says)."
"1962","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates, “I asked the Prophet (PBUH) that my wife has twenty shekels worth of jewellery. One of the narrators of this tradition, Yahya bin Abu Anisa, is obsolete, and this tradition is illusory. It is true that this tradition is transmitted and suspended."
"1963","Ibrahim Nakhai narrates that the wife of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) asked her about a necklace of hers which was twenty shekels and was made of gold. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) answered yes! How much did this woman ask? So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) replied five dirhams. This lady inquired whether I should pay this to such and such a person. This lady inquired about her nephew who was an orphan and was being raised by this lady."
"1964","Ibrahim Nakhai narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud's wife had jewelry. This woman asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may I pay her zakat. He answered yes! The woman asked if I should give this to my orphaned nephew. He said yes!"
"1965","Ali bin Salim narrates that I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik about jewelry, and he said that Zakat is not obligatory on it."
"1966","According to Nafi, one of the daughters of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was given 1,000 dirhams. This woman made jewelry for her, which amounted to four hundred dinars."
"1967","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that Zakat is not required on jewelry."
"1968","Nafee narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) made jewelry worth four dinars for his daughters, but Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) did not pay their zakat."
"1969","It has been narrated about Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) that she made gold ornaments for her daughters and did not pay their Zakat. The value of these ornaments was around fifty thousand."
"1970","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to give a sermon to the people."
"1971","Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Protect the property of orphans, do not deprive them of Zakat."
"1972","Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Zakat will be required on the property of an orphan."
"1973","Saeed bin Musaib narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said this: Take care of the wealth of the orphans and do not deprive them of Zakat."
"1974","Ibn Abu Rafi' narrated that the wealth of these people was with Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. When Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, returned the property to them, these people found some deficiency in it. Then, when they calculated it with the Zakat, they found it complete. Those people came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with them, said, ""Did you people think that I would have wealth and I would not pay Zakat on it?"""
"1975","The sons of Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) gave some land to Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) as a landholder. took possession of this wealth, so they counted their wealth and found it less. They came to Sayyidna Ali (RA) and told him about it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) inquired whether you have calculated his Zakat. The narrator narrates that these people calculated his zakat and found it fulfilled, then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said, ""You people thought that I would have some wealth and I would not pay its zakat."""
"1976","Narrated by Nafee, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) had the property of an orphan."
"1977","Ubaid bin Umayr narrates that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said this: Take care of the property of the orphans and do not deprive them of Zakat."
"1978","Nafi narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to pay Zakat on the property of an orphan."
"1979","Mujahid narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) gave some land to his slave Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) and he could not take care of it. That when the children of Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (RA) grew up, Sayyidna 'Ali (RA) found the wealth less. He replied, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, calculate his Zakat. When he calculated it, he found it."
"1980","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated that Sayyiduna Ali (RA) paid zakat on the property of the children of Sayyidna Abu Rafa’ (RA)."
"1981","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on the property of a minor. The narrator of this tradition, Ibn Lahiyyah, is not considered authentic."
"1982","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather about his father: A woman from Yemen came to the Prophet's service with her daughter. In her hands were two rings made of gold. The Prophet asked, ""Have you paid her zakat?"" He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Would you like it if Allah, the Exalted, clothed you with two bracelets of fire?”"
"1983","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, we have found this in the writings of Sayyiduna Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this about the zakat of camels. For five camels, one goat must be paid; for ten camels, two goats must be paid; for fifteen camels, three goats must be paid; for twenty, four goats must be paid; for twenty-five goats, payment must be made; then when they are more, then the payment of a daughter will be required among them. The payment of Lubun will be required, then if it is even more than one, it will be necessary to pay one Haqq for them. If there is more than one of them, one jazaa must be paid for every forty, and one haqqa must be paid for every fifty."
"1984","Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, among others; and al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā and al-Faḍl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbdillāh, from Anas, that when Abū Bakr was appointed as khalīfah, he dispatched Anas ibn Mālik to al-Baḥrayn and wrote for him this document: ""This is the obligatory charity (ṣadaqah) that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, imposed upon the Muslims, which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever among the believers is asked for it in its proper form, let him give it; and whoever is asked for more than that, let him not give it. For twenty-four camels or fewer, the obligation falls upon sheep: for every five, one sheep. When they reach twenty-five up to thirty-five, the due is a bint makhāḍ (a female camel in its second year). When they reach thirty-six up to forty-five, the due is a bint labūn (a female camel in its third year). When they reach forty-six up to sixty, the due is a ḥiqqah (a female camel in its fourth year, capable of being mounted). When they reach sixty-one up to seventy-five, the due is a jadhaʿah (a female camel in its fifth year). When they reach seventy-six up to ninety, the due are two bint labūn. When they reach ninety-one up to one hundred and twenty, the due are two ḥiqqah capable of being mounted. When they exceed one hundred and twenty, for every forty, a bint labūn is due, and for every fifty, a ḥiqqah. If the ages of the camels differ regarding the obligatory charity dues, then for one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a jadhaʿah but he does not have a jadhaʿah and has a ḥiqqah, the ḥiqqah shall be accepted from him, and he shall add with it two sheep if they are readily available to him, or twenty dirhams. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he does not have a ḥiqqah and has a jadhaʿah, the jadhaʿah shall be accepted from him, and the collector (muṣaddiq) shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he has only a bint labūn, the bint labūn shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have a bint labūn and has a ḥiqqah, the ḥiqqah shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have one and has a bint makhāḍ, the bint makhāḍ shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he does not have one and has a bint labūn, the bint labūn shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. If he does not have a bint makhāḍ in its proper form but has an ibn labūn (a male camel in its third year), it shall be accepted from him and nothing additional shall be required with it. Whoever has only four camels, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. When the camels reach five, one sheep is due. The ṣadaqah on freely grazing sheep: when they are forty up to one hundred and twenty, one sheep is due. When they exceed one hundred and twenty up to two hundred, two sheep are due. When they exceed two hundred up to three hundred, three sheep are due. When they exceed three hundred, for every hundred, one sheep is due. No decrepit animal, no defective animal, and no male goat shall be taken as ṣadaqah unless the collector so chooses. Separate flocks shall not be combined, nor shall a combined flock be separated, out of fear of the ṣadaqah. Whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle between them on an equal basis. If a man's freely grazing sheep fall short of forty by one, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. On silver (riqqah), the rate is one-quarter of one-tenth (2.5%). If one's wealth amounts to only one hundred and ninety dirhams, there is no ṣadaqah upon it unless the owner volunteers."" Yūsuf said in his narration: ""Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq wrote for him this document when he dispatched him to al-Baḥrayn: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is the obligatory charity.'"" Al-Faḍl ibn Sahl said: ""When Abū Bakr was appointed khalīfah, he dispatched Anas ibn Mālik to al-Baḥrayn and wrote for him this document, and sealed it with the seal of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The inscription on the seal of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was: 'Muḥammad' on one line, 'Rasūl' on one line, and 'Allāh' on one line. This is the obligatory charity that Allah imposed upon the Muslims, which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded."""
"1985","Dalaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Shīrawayh narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh informed us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: ""We took this document from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Anas, who narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: 'These are the obligatory charities of the Muslims which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever among the believers is asked for it, let him give it in its proper form; and whoever is asked for it in an improper form, let him not give it. For every twenty-four camels or fewer, the obligation falls upon sheep: for every five, one sheep. For twenty-five up to thirty-five, a bint makhāḍ is due; if no bint makhāḍ is available, then an ibn labūn (male) is given. For thirty-six up to forty-five, a bint labūn is due. For forty-six up to sixty, a ḥiqqah is due. For sixty-one up to seventy-five, a jadhaʿah is due. For seventy-six up to ninety, two bint labūn are due. For ninety-one up to one hundred and twenty, two ḥiqqah are due. For one hundred and twenty-one onward, for every forty, a bint labūn is due, and for every fifty, a ḥiqqah. If the ages of the camels differ, and the ṣadaqah due upon him is a jadhaʿah but he does not have a jadhaʿah and has a ḥiqqah, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall add with it two sheep if they are readily available, or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he does not have one and has a jadhaʿah, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due upon him is a ḥiqqah but he has only a bint labūn, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have a bint labūn and has a ḥiqqah, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have one and has a bint makhāḍ, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he has only a bint labūn, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he does not have one and has an ibn labūn (male), it shall be taken from him and nothing additional shall be required. Whoever has only four camels, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. When the camels reach five, one sheep is due. On freely grazing sheep: when they are forty up to one hundred and twenty, one sheep is due. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one up to two hundred, two sheep are due. When they exceed by one up to three hundred, for every hundred, one sheep is due. No decrepit animal, no defective animal, and no male goat shall be taken as ṣadaqah unless the collector so chooses. Separate flocks shall not be combined, nor shall a combined flock be separated, out of fear of the ṣadaqah. Whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle between them on an equal basis. If the freely grazing sheep fall short of forty by one, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. On silver, the rate is one-quarter of one-tenth. If one's wealth amounts to only one hundred and ninety dirhams, there is no ṣadaqah upon it unless the owner volunteers."" This chain of narration is sound (ṣaḥīḥ), and all its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt)."
"1986","Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: ""This is a copy of the document of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, which he wrote regarding charity, and it was in the possession of the family of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb."" Ibn Shihāb said: ""Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar read it to me, and I memorized it as it was. It is the same copy that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz transcribed from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar and Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh when he was appointed governor of al-Madīnah. He instructed his officials to act according to it and wrote with it to al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, and al-Walīd instructed his officials to act according to it. Thereafter, the caliphs continued to command accordingly. Then Hishām ibn Hānīʾ ordered it to be copied and sent to every Muslim official, commanding them to act by it and not to transgress it."" This is the document explaining its contents: ""No charity is taken from camels until they reach five. When they reach five, one sheep is due, up to ten. When they reach ten, two sheep are due, up to fifteen. When they reach fifteen, three sheep are due, up to twenty. When they reach twenty, four sheep are due, up to twenty-five. When they reach twenty-five, the obligation is established: a bint makhāḍ is due. If no bint makhāḍ is found, an ibn labūn (male) is given, up to thirty-five. When they reach thirty-six, a bint labūn is due, up to forty-five. When they reach forty-six, a ḥiqqah capable of being mounted is due, up to sixty. When they reach sixty-one, a jadhaʿah is due, up to seventy-five. When they reach seventy-six, two bint labūn are due, up to ninety. When they reach ninety-one, two ḥiqqah capable of being mounted are due, up to one hundred and twenty. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one, three bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and twenty-nine. When they reach one hundred and thirty, a ḥiqqah and two bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and thirty-nine. When they reach one hundred and forty, two ḥiqqah and a bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and forty-nine. When they reach one hundred and fifty, three ḥiqqah are due, up to one hundred and fifty-nine. When they reach one hundred and sixty, four bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and sixty-nine. When they reach one hundred and seventy, a ḥiqqah and three bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and seventy-nine. When they reach one hundred and eighty, two ḥiqqah and two bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and eighty-nine. When they reach one hundred and ninety, three ḥiqqah and a bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and ninety-nine. When they reach two hundred, four ḥiqqah or five bint labūn are due—whichever ages are found shall be taken according to the enumeration we have written in this document. Thereafter, everything regarding camels shall be taken according to what we have written in this document. No charity is taken from sheep until they reach forty. When they reach forty, one sheep is due, up to one hundred and twenty. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one, two sheep are due, up to two hundred. When they reach two hundred and one, three sheep are due, up to three hundred. When they exceed three hundred by one sheep, only three sheep are due until they reach four hundred. When they reach four hundred, four sheep are due, up to five hundred. When they reach five hundred, five sheep are due, up to six hundred. When they reach six hundred, six sheep are due, up to seven hundred. When they reach seven hundred, seven sheep are due, up to eight hundred. When they reach eight hundred, eight sheep are due, up to nine hundred. When they reach nine hundred, nine sheep are due, up to one thousand. When they reach one thousand, ten sheep are due. Thereafter, for every additional hundred, one sheep is due."""
"1987","Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman narrates that when Sayyiduna Umar bin Abdul Aziz was appointed as the caliph, he sent a message to Madinah asking them to look for a ruling on Zakat related to the time of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam). Similarly, the family of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) found the letter of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he wrote to his officials about Zakat and it was in accordance with what is written in the letter of the Prophet (PBUH) that the Prophet (PBUH) sent to Sayyidna Umar Bin Hazm (RA). Umar bin Abdul Aziz ordered his officials about Zakat to receive it in the light of these two letters. About the Zakat of camels, the same thing was written in both of them that if their number exceeds ninety one, it will be necessary to pay two Haqq among them. This ruling is up to twenty-one."
"1988","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Saeed narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri, may God be pleased with him): My mother sent me to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. ""He who asks for something from another even though he has one ounce (of silver) with him, then he has transgressed (Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him) I thought that my camel or Qoota was worth more than an ounce, so I came back, ""I did not ask you for anything."""
"1989","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a prosperous person and a person of high status."
"1990","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a person who is prosperous and a companion."
"1991","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1992","This tradition is narrated along with another document, but there is a difference of one word in it."
"1993","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that zakat (wealth) came in the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and people came to serve him."
"1994","Ubaidullah bin Adi narrates that two people told me this: ""Both of them came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the farewell Hajj and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for some of the Zakat money that he had."" I give it to both of you. It is not permissible to give it to a wealthy person and a person who has the ability to earn."
"1995","Sayyidna Qubaysa bin Makhariq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him for help for Hamala. And then he asks from someone, 'When he makes this payment, then he does not take anything.' A person whose (production) suffers a calamity and he wastes his property.' Belonging to 'They should bear witness that it is now begging for this person (so only these people can beg) besides it, begging will be haram.'"
"1996","Sayyidna Qubaysa bin Makhariq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I had to make a payment. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to seek his help in this matter. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We will make the payment on your behalf and remove it from the charity camels. Begging is forbidden 'Only three people can beg' 'A person who has to pay something, it becomes permissible to beg for him until he pays the payment and then stops after that' A person who is in dire need and hunger until three wise men of his nation testify to this (here the narrator is doubtful 'maybe this is such a word)' state that it is permissible for him to beg in such need and need even For him to be able to meet his needs and for a person who befalls a calamity and wastes his wealth, it is permissible for such a person to beg until he is able to meet his needs, then he stops after that."
"1997","Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is not permissible for a wealthy person to ask for anything from anyone. Only five people have a different ruling. Seen as a gift."
"1998","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1999","Sayyiduna Ali (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever asks for something even though he is prosperous, he increases the punishment of Hell through this act. He said, O Messenger of Allah! What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The dinner should be available. The narrator named Umar bin Khalid is obsolete."
"2000","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who, even though he is prosperous, begs from people, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his face will have a stain (the narrator has doubts about a single word here). What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fifty dirhams or as much gold as their value. A narrator named Ibn Aslam is weak."
"2001","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a person who has fifty dirhams in his possession. The name of the narrator Abu Shiba is Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq and it is weak."
"2002","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever, despite being prosperous, asks the people, “When he comes on the Day of Resurrection, there will be a scar on his face.” What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Whether it is a dirham or as much gold as their value."""
"2003","According to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA), this raiyat is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains the words fifty dirhams. Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him, narrates that in the first hadith, the narrator is delusional, he has quoted it with reference to Abu Ishaq, this is Sahib Hakeem bin Jubeer, and he is weak."
"2004","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who asks someone for something even though he is prosperous, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his face will be stained (the narrator has doubts about a word here). What does prosperity mean? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fifty dirhams or as much gold as its value (to be present)."
"2005","Hasan bin Saad narrates this statement of his father, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah (bin Masoud), may Allah be pleased with them, say that it is not permissible for a person to ask for anything from anyone who has fifty dirhams or gold equivalent to their value."
"2006","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the payment of zakat. He was told by Ibn Jameel, Khalid bin Waleed and Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib refused to pay the zakat. My armor and all my equipment is devoted to the cause of Allah Ta'ala. As far as Mr. Abbas is concerned, this payment is my responsibility and I will also pay him the same amount."
"2007","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect Zakat, but Ibn Jameel, Khalid bin Waleed and Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) refused to pay Zakat (when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told about this), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn Jameel did this because he was poor, then Allah made him prosperous as far as Khalid is concerned. So you have abused him because he has already dedicated his armor and equipment in the way of Allah. As for Sayyiduna Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah. His payment will be on me and the same amount will be paid with him."
"2008","Sayyiduna Ali (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abbas (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether he could pay Zakat on his wealth before the specified time had passed. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed them to do so."
"2009","It is narrated along with another document that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: We had received the Zakat of this year from Sayyiduna Abbas (may God be pleased with him) last year."
"2010","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that we had received his Zakat from Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) last year."
"2011","Sayyiduna Talha (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O Umar! Do you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father? We were in need of some property at that time, so we had already received Zakat on the property of Sayyiduna Abbas two years ago. The authenticity of this tradition has been contradicted by the narrator named Hakam. It is Sahih."
"2012","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (SAW) sent Sayyiduna Umar (RA) to collect Zakat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) had already given us the Zakat for this year and the next year."
"2013","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Umar (RA) to collect Zakat. When he returned, he complained about Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) and said that he did not pay his Zakat to me. Do you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father? Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) had already paid two years of Zakat together. The narrator has quoted the name of another narrator as Ubaidullah bin Umar, but what he meant was that this hadith was narrated from Muhammad bin Ubaidullah, ""Allah knows the rest."""
"2014","Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyidna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect Zakat and during this he had some disagreement with Sayyidna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Don't you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father?"" Sayyidna Abbas had already given us this year's Zakat last year."
"2015","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Try to escape Hellfire by means of a piece of date-palm, because it acts as a barrier for a hungry person as it does for a well-watered person."
"2016","Sayyida Fatima bin Qays (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that there is a right to wealth in addition to zakat. Then the Prophet (PBUH) recited this verse: ""Goodness is not only this. Turn your faces away."" This verse is valid till the end."
"2017","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2018","Abu Amrub bin Hamas narrates this statement of his father: I used to sell curry and quiver. Once, Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, passed by me and he said to me, pay zakat on your wealth. I said: O Commander of the Faithful! It is in the sally, so he said, you estimate its value, then pay its zakat."
"2019","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him). The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this about a horse."
"2020","Haritha bin Muzarab narrates that some people from Egypt came to the service of Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them. They told us that we have received some land and some slaves. We want them to pay their zakat. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, said, ""What my two masters before me did not do, I will not do that until I consult about it."" So they all declared it right. Sayyidna Ali remained silent. Sayyidna Umar said, O Abul Hasan! Why are you not talking? So Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: What these men have advised you is right, but it is important that it is not a tax that they will have to pay even after you. Sayyidna Umar (RA) collected 10 dirhams from a slave and ordered him to provide two acres of wheat as food per month. 5 dirhams were received from the mule and 5 jirabs were required to be given as monthly food. A narrator named Abu Ishaq says that during the time of Hajj, it was collected from us but our share was not paid."
"2021","A narrator named Haritha narrates that some people from Syria came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar, they told us that we have acquired some property, which are horses and slaves. Sayyiduna Ali (RA) was also included in it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, ""It is fine if it is not considered as a tribute that will continue to be collected from him even after him."""
"2022","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have forgiven you the zakat of horses and slaves, and no zakat will be required for less than two hundred (dirhams)."
"2023","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat will not be required on a horse and a slave."
"2024","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, ""There is no obligation to give charity to a slave."
"2025","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that a man's horse and his slave will not be required to pay any kind of charity (i.e. Zakat)."
"2026","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that Zakat is not required on a Muslim man's mare, his slave and his maidservant. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2027","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed this Sunnah regarding the dowry of women that it should be twelve ounces and one ounce is worth forty dirhams, so it will be four hundred and eighty dirhams in total, and the Prophet of Allah has also set this limit. has also established this Sunnah which is produced from the land i.e. Wheat, Barley, Raisins, Dates. When these are five wasaqs, one wasaq is of sixty Sa'as, then it will be three Saas in total which will be according to this Sa'as which are related to the Sunnah. This hadith has been narrated only by Saleh bin Musa with regard to Mansoor and this person is weak in hadeeth."
"2028","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has established this Sunnah: ""Zakat will not be required on grains less than five wasaqs."""
"2029","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not required on five ounces (of silver), Zakat is not required on less than five camels, and Zakat is not required on grains less than five Wasq. (The narrator narrates) A wasaq is sixty sa's."
"2030","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if (the land) is found in Baal, it is necessary to pay a tenth of it (translated)."
"2031","Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) about the land irrigated by the sky (i.e. rain) through canals and springs, and the land irrigated (i.e. naturally irrigated), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed ushar (i.e. the payment of one-tenth of the produce) and on that which is irrigated (artificially) he has prescribed half-ushar (i.e. the payment of one-twentieth)."
"2032","Salim bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has prescribed the payment of one-tenth (of the produce of the land) that is irrigated through the Baal (underground irrigation of a tree near water), sky, canal, spring, and that which is artificially irrigated will require the payment of half-usher."
"2033","Sayyiduna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed one-tenth of the land that does not need irrigation and the land that is irrigated by rain, canals and springs, and one-twentieth of the land that is irrigated with water from wells."
"2034","Narrator Abu Bakr-Nami has narrated this. Shaykh Rabi' has narrated this. I have heard Imam Shafi'i saying, 'The word ""Al-Baal"" used in tradition means the one whose roots reach the water."
"2035","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that the land that is irrigated by rain or spring will be required to pay usher, and that which is irrigated through a dole (i.e. by artificial means), it will be required to pay half usher."
"2036","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a letter to the people of Yemen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote this letter to Harith Abdul Kalal and his other companions living in Yemen, who belonged to Maafir and Hamdan. of the produce) shall be required to pay one-twentieth."
"2037","Abu Zubayr says: He heard Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “The land that is irrigated by a spring will require the payment of one-tenth, and the land that is irrigated by the Saniya will require the payment of half-tithe."
"2038","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave an order about Zakat, and a man brought raw dates. (Narrated by the narrators) Whoever brought anything, that thing was attributed to the person who brought it, so this verse was revealed about it, ""And do not intend to spend it on something worthless."" The narrator states that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that 'Jarur and Lon al-Muhabiq should be received in Zakat."
"2039","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2040","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two types of dates (to receive as Zakat) Jaar War and Lon Ahabiq. The narrator narrates that some people used to deliberately take their bad fruits and pay them in zakat, so they were forbidden to pay these two kinds of dates. This is why this verse was revealed: ""And do not intend to spend it on something worthless."" This tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions."
"2041","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that some people used to pay the bad fruits of their fruits as Zakat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking or paying two kinds of dates as Zakat. Some narrators have also copied this tradition as a Mursal tradition."
"2042","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this verse in which Allah Ta'ala has said, ""And do not intend to spend it on something worthless."""
"2043","Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to estimate the grape trees of the Thaqif tribe by how much fruit is on them. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2044","Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharma (may God be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Atab bin Usayd (may God be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the grape trees of the Thaqif tribe should be assessed in the same way as date trees (fruits on them) are assessed."
"2045","The same hadith is narrated from Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd along with another chain of transmission. Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered grapes to be valued as dates are valued and their zakat was collected in the form of minqi, just as the zakat of palm trees is collected in the form of dates. Some other narrators have followed in narrating it."
"2046","Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about the zakat of grapes: it will be assessed in the same way as a date tree (fallen dates) is assessed, and then its zakat will be paid in the form of raisins (yaminqi), just as the zakat of a date tree is paid in the form of dates. Follow up."
"2047","Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this about the zakat of grapes, then after that he narrated according to the previous hadith."
"2048","Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send a person to these people to estimate the production of grapes and fruits of the youth (and Zakat was collected based on this calculation)."
"2049","Sayyiduna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that Zakat be collected in the form of grapes by calculating the yield of a grape tree, just as dates are estimated (or dates are collected by estimation)."
"2050","Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when Allah gave the land of Khyber to His Messenger as wealth, His Messenger allowed them (Jews) to stay there and made an agreement that the produce there would be (divided equally) between those Jews and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). You are the most disliked of Allah's creations to me. You copied the Prophets of Allah. You attributed falsehood to Allah. But my dislike of you will not induce me to do anything wrong with you. So they said: Because of this (justice and justice) the heavens and the earth are established. We collect from this account. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Radiyallahu Anhu said, ""Take out (i.e., pay) me this production."""
"2051","Sayyiduna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) ordered that Zakat be collected in the form of grapes by calculating the yield of a grape tree, just as dates are estimated (or dates are collected by estimation)."
"2052","Sayyida Aisha (RA) was once mentioning about Khyber. She said that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Rawaha (RA) to the Jews. When the fruit was ready, he estimated the yield of the palm trees. Then he gave the Jews the option to collect according to this estimate or pay them according to this estimate. The Prophet (PBUH) ordered to estimate. Zakat should be calculated before the fruit is ready and separated. This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira along with another chain of transmission."
"2053","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission regarding Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa."
"2054","Sayyidna Sahl bin Hatmah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to make an estimate. Abu Hathmah has imposed more payment on us while estimating. So the Prophet called him and said: Your cousin has to say, ""You have made more payment on him in estimating"" (says the narrator). I said, O Messenger of Allah! I have left so many more dates for him, so that he can feed his family and the poor, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your cousin has given you more and has acted justly."""
"2055","Sayyiduna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him to guide me to an action that would bring me closer to Paradise and keep me away from Hell! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “If you shorten the speech, avoid asking, ‘Free the slave,’ free the neck (free the slave or the slave girl).” He said, O Messenger of Allah! Aren't these two the same? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! Freeing the soul means that you free it and freeing the neck means that you help it to pay its price 'Give the high-yielding (camel or goat) free of charge and keep the relationship with the abusive relative' If you cannot do this, speak only good things with your tongue."
"2056","Abu Ahmad Zubair says that Sufyan Al-Thawri came and asked him about this hadith. I was there at that time. The narrator has a doubt, 'Perhaps these are the words. Sufyan al-Thawri came to me and asked me about this hadith."
"2057","This same tradition is narrated along with another document, but these words are added in it: feed the hungry, feed the thirsty, enjoin good and forbid evil."
"2058","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu’adh (RA) to Yemen and said, “When you go to the People of the Book, invite them to bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah.” Tell them that Allah has made zakat obligatory on them in their wealth, which will be given from the wealthy to the poor. If they accept your words about this, then avoid accepting the good wealth of the people and avoid the curse of the oppressed, because there is no veil between him (and Allah)."
"2059","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Mu'adh (RA) to Yemen, he said to him, ""Are you going to the People of the Book?"" The first thing you should invite them to do is to 'confess the oneness of Allah Ta'ala. When they come to know this, you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made five daily prayers obligatory on them. When they know this, you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made five daily prayers obligatory on them, and you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made Zakat of their wealth obligatory on them. It will be given from the wealthy people to their poor people. If they acknowledge this, then you will receive it and avoid receiving people's (especially) good wealth."
"2060","Aun bin Abu Huhaifa narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person who collected zakat to us. He collected zakat from our prosperous people and then distributed it among our poor people."
"2061","Aun bin Abu Huhaifah narrates this statement of his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his servants to us, in which he collected zakat from our wealthy people and gave it to our poor people. I was an orphan (adult) boy at that time."
"2062","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says that Zakat money will not be transferred from one city to another, but it can be done to give a loan to relatives. This tradition is discontinued."
"2063","Sayyidna Ziyad bin Harith al-Sadai (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), ‘He (PBUH) was about to send an army to my people at that time.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Stop your army. I guarantee you that those people will accept Islam and obey. I write a letter to my people, they will come accepting Islam and obey. The narrator says, ""I didn't ask for the people who believe in him!"" Rather, Allah Ta'ala has favored these people and has blessed them with guidance. Narrator narrates: Then a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) and asked the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) for the amount of Zakat. The Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said to him: Allah, the Exalted, is not satisfied with the decision of any Prophet or any other person regarding Zakat until that person divides this Zakat into eight parts."
"2064","Sayyidna Haritha bin Muzarab (RA) narrates that some people from Syria came to the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA) and they told us that they had left some property and got slaves. A narrator named Ishaq has quoted these words: ""I will do what has been done by those before me."" Then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) consulted the people about it. ""Among the people who consulted, Sayyidna Ali (RA) was included."" A narrator named Isaac quotes these words if it is not placed in the order that the wallaby receives it after you (so that's fine). (The narrator says) So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) made the payment of one dinar obligatory for a horse."
"2065","Asim bin Zamra narrates that some people from Syria brought horses and slaves. They said to Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them: You should collect their Zakat. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, said, ""According to my knowledge, no one has done this before me. I will inquire about it."""
"2066","Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa Radiyallahu Anhu narrates, ""He has narrated this matter as a hadeeth"" (that is, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said), ""Whatever Allah has made lawful in His book, is lawful, and what He has made forbidden, is forbidden, and what He has not mentioned is a health."" The matter is not forgotten (does not forget). Then he recited this verse. ""And your Lord is not forgetful."""
"2067","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sadaqah al-Fitr is a means of purification for the fasting person, and it is given to a poor person as food. No one is hurt in the words of this tradition."
"2068","Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) quotes this statement of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father (Sayyidna Imam Hussain, peace be upon him). So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is obligatory on every small, big, free, slave, and Muslim.”"
"2069","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered every Muslim, whether he is free or slave, minor or adult, to pay one saa of dates or one saa of jujube."
"2070","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but the word ""Muslims"" is added in it."
"2071","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ordered every Muslim, whether he is a slave or free, male or female, minor or adult, to pay one Saa of dates or one Saa of dates as Sadaqah Fitr after Ramadan."
"2072","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has made it obligatory to give one Sa'a of dates or one Sa'a of dates, which is to be paid as Sadaqah Fitr to every slave or free, male and female, minor and adult Muslim."
"2073","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has ordered that every Muslim, whether he is young or old, should pay one saa of dates or one saa of barley in the charity of Fitr."
"2074","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every free and slave Muslim, which is a saa of dates or a saa of jujube."
"2075","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has made it obligatory for every Muslim to pay one Saa of dates as Sadaqah Fitr, after which the narrator mentioned the entire hadith."
"2076","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) made obligatory on every Muslim, free or slave, male or female, one saa of dates or one saa of dates as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"2077","Imam Ali Raza (may Allah be pleased with him) and Imam Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to his father (Imam Jafar Sadiq may God bless him and grant him peace) and his grandfather (Imam Muhammad Baqir may God bless him and grant him peace) with reference to his forefathers and forefathers (i.e. Imam Zain al-Abidin, Imam Hussain and Sayyiduna Ali may God bless him and grant him peace) narrate this saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made it obligatory to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr on every young and old woman who is under his protection."
"2078","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has ordered to give Sadaqah-e-Fitrada on behalf of every young and old, free and slave, who are under your care. A narrator named Qasim has narrated it as a marfu' hadith, 'this narrator is not strong and it is true that this hadith is suspended."
"2079","Nafi' narrated this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he used to give Sadaqah Fitrada on behalf of all his family members, including all the people who were dependent on him, he also used to give Sadaqah Fitrada on behalf of his slaves and the slaves of his wives."
"2080","Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace be upon him) sent a person to announce this announcement in the streets of Mecca."
"2081","Amro bin Shuaib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person who announced in a loud voice in the valley of Makkah, “Remember to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr (it is obligatory).” After that, the narrator narrated the previous hadith, “however, these words are extra in it. It is obligatory for every citizen and villager.”"
"2082","Amro bin Shuaib narrates that I have come to know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a person who made this announcement to every Muslim (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith)."
"2083","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a person to announce that Sadaqah al-Fitr is Haqq and that every man, woman, freed slave, citizen, villager, Muslim must give it from a prah, which will be half a day of wheat and a day of date palm."
"2084","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered a person to make this announcement in a valley in the valley of Makkah. However, in this tradition, these words are added, remember that children belong to the bed and the adulterer gets deprivation."
"2085","Ata states that there will be two days of wheat and one day of dates and one sa' of dates."
"2086","Kathir bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory for every Muslim to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr, which is a Saa of dates, or a Saa of raisins, or a Saa of cheese, or a Saa of jaggery."
"2087","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the Prophet (SAW) ordered every citizen and inhabitant, small and large, free and slave, to give a saa of dates, a saa of barley or a maund of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"2088","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that Sadaqah al-Fitr will be one saa of dates or two maads of wheat and it will be paid by every free slave."
"2089","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has made Ramadan charity obligatory for every male, female, free and slave, which will be a saa of dates or a saa of grain."
"2090","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encouraged everyone to give charity in Ramadan (i.e. Sadaqah al-Fitr) which is a saa of dates or a saa of wheat or a saa of wheat. A narrator of this tradition is not Bakrban Asudaqvi."
"2091","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we have been commanded that we should pay Ramadan charity (i.e. Sadaqah al-Fitr) from every free slave, one Saa of grain. will be done Narrator states, I think, 'There are also these words in the hadith, the person who will pay the dough will be accepted by him and the person who will do satvadaka will be accepted by him."
"2092","Kathir bin Abdullah narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has made it obligatory for every man, woman, slave or free to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"2093","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) prescribed a saa of dates and a saa of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr. The narrator has also quoted these words. It is obligatory on every free and slave, male and female Muslim."
"2094","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm to receive half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates."
"2095","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), people used to give a saa of wheat or a saa of dates or a saa of raisins as Sadaqah al-Fitr. When the time of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) came, wheat became abundant, so he set half a sa' of wheat in place of all these things."
"2096","This tradition has been narrated along with some other evidences. In one tradition, these words are mentioned. People mentioned before him the charity of Fitr. He said: I will give the same charity of Fitr that I used to pay during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It will be a saa of dates or raisins, a saa of wheat or a saa of barley or a saa of cheese. Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri said no! This is the price set by Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) 'I will not accept it nor will I follow it."
"2097","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says: “We used to give Sadaqah-e-Fitr on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr, which was one Sa’a of grain or one Sa’a of dates or one Sa’a of barley or one Sa’a of raisins or one Sa’a of raisins. He gave a sermon to the people on the pulpit of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and while mentioning Sadaqah al-Fitr, he explained that I believe that a handful of wheat in the evening is equal to one saa of dates. Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that at that time people first mentioned Domad."
"2098","The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it these words are a saa of grain."
"2099","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to pay one saa of flour or one saa of dates or one saa of wheat or one saa of raisins or one saa of barley or one saa of cheese."
"2100","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to him about Sadaqah al-Fitr: It will be a saa of raisins or a saa of dates or a saa of cheese or a saa of flour."
"2101","Malik bin Aws narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give one Saa of grain in Sadaqah al-Fitr. Narrator states that in those days, our grains were wheat, dates, sorghum and cheese."
"2102","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2103","Abdullah bin Thaalbah narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Sadaqa al-Fitr, one Sa'a of dates, one Sa'a of wheat, and half a Sa'a of wheat, should be paid by men and women, free and slave."
"2104","Abdullah bin Thaalbah narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “From every human being, give a sa’a of wheat from every person, small and large, male and female, from the prosperous and the poor."
"2105","Tha'albah bin Abu Sa'eer narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: He paid a sa'a of wheat (the narrator has doubts about a word here) Pay from every small and big, male and female, free and slave, prosperous and poor. Allah will give him more than that."
"2106","This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: ""As far as the poor are concerned, Allah will make him prosperous""."
"2107","Al-Zuhri narrates this statement of his father regarding Ibn Abu Saair: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Give a Saa of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr from every person, whether he is young or old, free or slave, male or female."
"2108","This hadith is also narrated along with another document."
"2109","Al-Zuhri narrates this statement of his father with reference to Abdullah bin Thaalbah: Once, while giving a sermon, the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered that every young and old, free and slave, should pay one saa of dates or one saa of barley as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"2110","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: Giving Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every wealthy and poor person."
"2111","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Thaalba (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon a day or two before Eid, he (PBUH) said, ""Every person will pay a sah of wheat in Sadaqah al-Fitr, or a sah of any kind of grain in addition to that."""
"2112","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) ordered the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr. He said, ""It will be one Sa'a of dates, or one Sa'a of wheat, or one Sa'a of wheat."""
"2113","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about Sadaqah al-Fitr: “It shall be paid by every small and great, free and slave” which is half a saa of wheat or a saa of dates. The narrator has narrated it as a marfu' hadith in the same way."
"2114","This same hadith has been transmitted as a muqaf tradition along with another chain of transmission and it is correct."
"2115","Asma bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sadaqah al-Fitr: it will consist of two saa of wheat, or one saa of barley, or one saa of dates, or one saa of raisins."
"2116","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) states that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every free and slave, male and female, young and old, poor and rich. The narrator narrates that Zahri has narrated this tradition as a marfu' hadith."
"2117","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon and said to us, “Whoever has this, he should give half a Sa’a of wheat or a Sa’a of dates or a Sa’a of barley or a Sa’a of flour or a Sa’a of wheat or a Sa’a of wheat (as Sadaqah Fitr). These words have been narrated by a narrator named Salman bin Arqam and this person is a dead hadith."
"2118","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Thaalbah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon to the people one day before Eid-ul-Fitr and said, ""One Sa'a of wheat should be performed by two men (here, the narrator has doubts about the wording of the hadith) or one Sa'a of date palm or one Sa'a of jujube should be performed by each free and slave, young and old."""
"2119","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sadaqa al-Fitr will be paid by every young and old, male and female, Jew and Christian (slave) free and slave, which is half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates or one saa of barley."
"2120","It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to pay sadaqah on behalf of everyone, young and old, male and female, free and slave, unbeliever and Muslim, and he even used to pay sadaqah al-fitr on behalf of his second-class slaves. One of the narrators of this tradition is Uthman."
"2121","Ata bin Abi Rabah says that a man will also give charity on behalf of his slave, even if that slave is a Magian."
"2122","Imam Abu Hanifa says that if you give alms (this is a special tree of India) in Sadaqah al-Fitr, it will also be permissible."
"2123","Bishr ibn Umar narrates, I requested Imam Malik to give me the Mad (specific measure) of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imam Malik asked for it. A slave brought it and he gave it to him. I showed it to Imam Malik and asked: Is this him? He answered yes! This is the measure of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said, “This is not the specific measure of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he himself used.” Rather, it is a measure according to his measurements (says the narrator). We pay according to this.' I said: A person wants to give Sadaqah al-Fitr or a kind of expiation according to Mud (whichever is greater, will it be paid)? He said: No! He should pay according to that amount, then after that he should pay as much as he wants."
"2124","Ishaq bin Salman narrates: I asked Imam Malik: O Abu Abdullah! What was the weight of the Prophet's Sa'a? So he replied, five pounds and one-third of a pound according to the Iraqi pound. I have measured it. I said: O Abu Abdullah! You have issued a fatwa against the elders of your time. They asked who they are. I said: Imam Abu Hanifa! Because they say that it is eight pounds, Imam Malik got angry and said: May Allah destroy them! What courage has he shown regarding Allah Ta'ala? Then he said to one of the people sitting there: O so-and-so! You come with your old majesty, oh so and so! You bring your uncle's saa, oh so-and-so! You bring your grandmother's saa. A narrator named Ishaq narrates that there various people gathered together, Imam Malik said; On what account do you preserve it? So he said that my father has narrated this matter regarding his father, he had paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this saa. The second gentleman said that my father has narrated this with reference to his brother, he had paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this saa. The third said: My father told me this. He narrated this from his mother. He paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this Saa. The narrator says: I said: O Abu Abdullah! I will tell you something even more surprising about him (i.e. Imam Abu Hanifa) 'He says that half a Sa'a will be paid in Sadaqah al-Fitr and one Sa'a is worth eight pounds', so Imam Malik said that this is even more surprising than before. We have heard the scholars of our city (Madinah) saying this in full."
